    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1061">

                <pb facs="0998" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.0665/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-17T15:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 17, 1915, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 18, 8.30 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>306. Your 71, November 25,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1061-f1"/> and your 262 of the
                    13th instant.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1061-f2"/> Note received from Foreign Office
                    stating that, owing to the extreme gravity of the present situation, decisions
                    now in force (enclosure No. 2, despatch 137, November 28<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1061-f3"/>) regarding restrictions of sealed official
                    correspondence cannot be changed. By these decisions military commanders of
                    districts where military movement is taking place are empowered to stop all
                    sealed official correspondence between consulates and embassy, etc. Will file
                    protest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
